From 59a00becc044a44e252f54c2abc00ce2251720eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: plotarmordev <299844489+plotarmordev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 11:12:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 14/30] engine_api: audio events, so a speech engine can
 publish PCM while it generates

A streamed speech request now receives audio events: each one hands the caller a final, rising prefix of the PCM
before the finished event. The Drama host decodes the first frame alone, for the earliest audio, then frames in
groups, and publishes each decoded prefix.
---
 zig/src/core/engine_api.zig           |  6 +++++-
 zig/src/core/lane_host_reuse_test.zig |  6 +++---
 zig/src/native/drama_host.zig         | 30 ++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 zig/src/server/mailbox.zig            |  2 ++
 zig/tests/qwen27/dflash_served.zig    |  2 +-
 zig/tests/qwen27/reuse.zig            |  2 +-
 zig/tests/qwen27/served.zig           |  2 +-
 7 files changed, 40 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

